- Outage Postmortem (2026-08-21)
    - Symptom: no daily brief commits since 2026-08-11 while GitHub Actions stayed green
    - Root cause: free model deepseek-v4-flash-free began failing on Aug 12 (429 rate limit, then permanent 400 "Model is unavailable"); translate_fa owned the only git commit, so nothing shipped
    - Amplifier 1: run_pipeline.py caught every stage exception and exited 0, masking failures in CI
    - Amplifier 2: editorial and summarize stages swallowed LLM errors internally, shipping unedited drafts marked as success
    - Fix: new primary model muse-spark-1.2-contributor-free (Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index 57), runtime failover chain nemotron-3-ultra-free / mimo-v2.5-free / hy3-free, decoupled EN/FA deploys, non-zero CI exit on critical stage failure, degraded flags in run_meta

- Backfill Completion (2026-08-21)
    - Editorial repairs: Aug 5 and Aug 9 rebuilt from their surviving headlines via repair_editorial prompt (attribution only, no invented facts or links); Aug 11 polished with the stock editorial prompt, all 7 links verified live
    - Date-scoped backfills: Aug 16 to Aug 20 published from items actually dated to each target day (kept 4/5/9/5/3 of 104 fetched), single-source France24 days by feed reality, not fabrication; Aug 1 to Aug 15 left as honest gaps since no feed retains that coverage
    - Farsi mirrors regenerated for all eight dates; mailer skipped every run by the today-only guard, zero emails sent for backfills
    - New tooling: scripts/repair_post.py, scripts/backfill_dates.py, filter_items_by_date in run_pipeline.py, prompts/repair_editorial.yaml, tests/test_backfill.py (58 tests passing)
    - Open issue: Reuters rss-bridge returns zero entries (DNS failure locally, empty feed on CI); source contributes nothing to daily briefs until resolved

- New Sources Added (2026-08-21)
    - Three reachable sources added after probing 15 candidates through the real fetcher: BBC Middle East, Jerusalem Post, Middle East Eye
    - Chosen for perspective balance against the existing Al Jazeera/France24/Euronews mix: mainstream Western (BBC), Israeli security-first (JPost), independent regional critical of intervention (MEE)
    - Blocked candidates rejected on evidence: Times of Israel 403 bot-blocked, Al Arabiya 403, AP hub 401, CNN stale since 2023, i24 returns HTML
    - Bias stubs seeded in source_biases.json and Farsi mirror so editorial bias detection can record observations from day one; FA display names translated per existing convention
    - Fetch smoke test with all seven sources: 185 items total, reuters still zero

